== SOURCE
l:B_ := { x_ y_ z -> x_ y_ z }
== TITLE
B, the Bluebird: composition
== NOTE l:B_
An exported name
`l:` marks a name the library exports; a program that imports it as `c:` writes `c:B_`. The underlined B makes it a function.
== NOTE x_ y_
Function parameters
An underlined letter makes a parameter a function, so the body can apply it.
== NOTE z
A value parameter
No underline: `z` is data. B takes x, then y, then z, one at a time (every function is curried).
== NOTE x_ y_ z #2
x (y z)
Right to left: y applied to z, then x applied to that. Composition: Dyalog `f⍤g` (or `f∘g`), J `f@:g`, BQN `f∘g`.
